// Code signing — shared base config.
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM is intentionally NOT set here. Each collaborator signs with
// their own Apple Developer team, and committing a team ID means every pull
// overwrites someone else's signing and breaks their build with
// "you don't have access to this membership resource".
//
// Instead, set YOUR team in Local.xcconfig (same folder, gitignored):
//
//     cp LyraMusicHost/Config/Local.xcconfig.example LyraMusicHost/Config/Local.xcconfig
//     # then edit Local.xcconfig and put in your Team ID
//
// Find your Team ID in Xcode → Settings → Accounts (select your team), or at
// https://developer.apple.com/account under Membership.
//
// Code-sign entitlements are also selectable per developer. The default uses the
// committed entitlements (which request the group.com.randll.lyra App Group, owned
// by the upstream account). A developer on a different Apple account that can't use
// that App Group can blank these in Local.xcconfig to build without it (widgets lose
// their shared data, but the app signs under a wildcard profile and keeps its data).
LYRA_HOST_ENTITLEMENTS = LyraMusicHost/LyraMusicHost.entitlements
LYRA_WIDGET_ENTITLEMENTS = LyraWidgets/LyraWidgets.entitlements

#include? "Local.xcconfig"
